{
  "note": "Cover images for taxonomy rows that are NOT model/part leaves — generation roots, generation waves, retail lines, brand rows and franchise rows. The 504 model/part leaves are covered separately by scripts/fetch-taxonomy-images.mjs and canonical-beys.json; this manifest is the branch-and-brand half that corpus cannot express, because a wave is not a model.",
  "sources": {
    "corpus": "A local read-only mirror of beyblade.fandom.com images at $BEY_CORPUS/linka/images/fandom/**. Resolved by FILENAME, so the hash-bucket directory layout is an implementation detail. Zero network calls — the bytes are already on disk.",
    "wiki": "A named `File:` on the given MediaWiki host, resolved via prop=imageinfo. 🛑 Pin the FILE, not the article. prop=pageimages returns the article's lead image, which on a company article is usually its headquarters building — The Pokemon Company resolved to a Tokyo skyscraper, Banpresto to an office tower, Dragon Ball to a file named SANY2051.jpg. Pinning the file also makes a wrong logo visible in a diff instead of only on the page."
  },
  "conventions": {
    "variant": "\"cover\" fills display.coverImage. \"hasbro\" fills hasbroCoverImage, the logo shown beside the 'Also known as' name.",
    "omission": "A taxonomy row absent from this file keeps whatever it already has (a seedPhoto placeholder tile, or nothing). That is deliberate: an honest gap beats a wrong or guessed image, the same rule the 25-of-220 uncovered models already follow."
  },
